<title>UK: Gale briefly shuts U.K. Forties crude terminal.</title>
<headline>Gale briefly shuts U.K. Forties crude terminal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Crude oil loadings at BP's Hound Point terminal in east Scotland were delayed on Wednesday because of gale force winds but the problem only lasted a few hours, a BP spokesman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;There was only one small ship affected,&quot; he said. &quot;It was due to tie up late last night and that was delayed for a few hours.. it is now due to load imminently,&quot; he said, but did not know the name or size of the ship.</p>
<p>All other loadings were proceeding as normal, he added. Lloyds shipping service reported gale force winds in the North Sea on Wednesday of up to 40 knots.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
